#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087397 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/id #uuid "021d25c6-08db-5f20-a89b-110389d08e29" :question/math-academy-id "e-3224" :question/problem "What is the equation of the circle given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/843/Source/Images/e0a6f6470cf511081c0dedf72450110f.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-1,1)$ and the radius of the circle is $r = 3$. Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - a)^{2} + (y - b)^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\n(x - (-1))^{2} + (y - 1)^{2} &= 3^{2} \\\\\n(x + 1)^{2} + (y - 1)^{2} &= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087399 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "e2d2147e-98df-54df-a271-4c5dff362a96" :question/math-academy-id "e-3226" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x-2)^2 + (y+4)^2 = 9$?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - a)^{2} + (y - b)^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + (y + 4)^{2} &= 9 \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + (y - (-4))^{2} &= 3^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a = 2$, $b =-4$, and $r = 3$.\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,-4)$ and its radius is $3$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087400 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/id #uuid "7e01a50d-62f1-5cc2-875e-bb085ef571c4" :question/math-academy-id "e-3230" :question/problem "The line segment $\\overline{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(3,4)$ and $(-1,2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/843/Source/Images/ceca3bcfb8d6dd7f7f3fdba448fe0f44.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(3,4)$ and $Y(-1,2)$, we find that the length the diameter is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nXY &= \\sqrt{(-1 - 3)^{2} + (2 - 4)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{20} \\\\\n&= 2\\sqrt{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is\n\n$$\nr = \\dfrac{XY}{2} = \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2}, \\dfrac {y_1+y_2}{2}\\right) = \\left(\\dfrac{3+(-1)}{2}, \\dfrac {4+2}{2}\\right)=(1,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius\n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{5}\n$$\n\nand center\n\n$$\n(a,b)=(1,3)\n$$\n\nand therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - a)^{2} + (y - b)^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} + (y - 3)^{2} &= (\\sqrt{5})^{2} \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} + (y - 3)^{2} &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/id #uuid "16faff9a-9599-5b8c-85cd-132f3e3f4b92" :question/math-academy-id "e-6150" :question/problem "The circle above is centered at $C(2, 0)$ and the point $X(-1, 4)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/843/Source/Images/d44b59e332071b7cc4d32a6ddee9b2fb.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^2 + (y-b)^2 = r^2\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nCX &= \\sqrt{(2 - (-1))^{2} + (0 - 4)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{3^{2} + 4^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{25} \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - a)^{2} + (y - b)^{2} &= r^{2} \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + (y - 0)^{2} &= 5^{2} \\\\\n(x - 2)^{2} + y^{2} &= 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267263 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48e24bd3-0c4b-500a-be85-f4cda556f1a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267265} {:answer/id #uuid "5913a424-f270-53b9-99e1-7685a800e2a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267266} {:answer/id #uuid "3ad1db0f-7139-5525-b700-3174ae2da42f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267267} {:answer/id #uuid "12698c95-295e-5010-b859-69c8ad5ac117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267268} {:answer/id #uuid "2495499f-d66f-5f01-9219-b852a552549a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5913a424-f270-53b9-99e1-7685a800e2a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267266} :answer-field/id #uuid "762ee684-a7e7-5101-af51-231304a26ee0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267264}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de5f5e5c-aac7-5af2-b684-be46251b0bf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-116929" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/b69a99c42bcdbd7e6ae3434862019b792da6bea498fd92a36595722d4fb66995.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={6}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267270 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6432d359-e4ca-5f87-bcae-5444801b3bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267272} {:answer/id #uuid "5c741fd6-9721-58dc-931b-9b99d124c051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267273} {:answer/id #uuid "db6df274-fac1-5d92-8e0f-7f54a6598b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267274} {:answer/id #uuid "31ba0c7b-a13a-5ff0-b52c-32140f647d55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267275} {:answer/id #uuid "9a276106-0072-5bc8-8b6e-5fe114cef85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db6df274-fac1-5d92-8e0f-7f54a6598b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267274} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d526b29-08cd-5de5-a128-b9bc96c6177e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267271}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c307ede6-e70a-59ee-90bc-a8a2eb56a1d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-117077" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/5e138922d95cbcf6cc6ceba4d7695b110f5414e08f2a5e9e2ae2d71bff70ab5d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(2,-3)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7dceb7b-7f1b-5eb2-ad2d-5aa8547d1f52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267279} {:answer/id #uuid "109182bc-9184-5579-8d5a-510ebc5c50f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267280} {:answer/id #uuid "14e35877-21ea-5c8e-a083-367597e18339" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267281} {:answer/id #uuid "7300c62a-0dec-5518-823b-094d612ce18f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267282} {:answer/id #uuid "0f5a75b0-6161-540a-9378-339739be7374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f5a75b0-6161-540a-9378-339739be7374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267283} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef45b709-177c-5e59-bd16-13bc3328423e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267278}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b54f74fb-eb0a-56d9-aa78-0fabf47d3d3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-117081" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/9839540667b095cec69ce6ea429aa99b129e90fee26c4adf1f25ffa6019d5067.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-5,0)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=7.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {(x-(-5))}^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={7}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c2a2bc2-b7dc-5476-8109-e1b67dadfdde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-7,-10)$ and the radius is $100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267286} {:answer/id #uuid "9cc046a8-1e8e-5b2a-8355-e48fc8fbaf7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267287} {:answer/id #uuid "f3efe93f-2f36-5e06-93ff-0697c3a6c441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(7,10)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267288} {:answer/id #uuid "64f09c47-0b3a-5fc5-90a3-8c24e88a3271" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-7,-10)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267289} {:answer/id #uuid "3b4a7ab8-a1ef-5b73-bcff-88df89302080" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(7,10)$ and the radius is $100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3efe93f-2f36-5e06-93ff-0697c3a6c441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(7,10)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267288} :answer-field/id #uuid "696faf1b-e6c2-51ff-8bb6-0e7211917002" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267285}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "064ec2a1-8603-5d8c-96f4-94b94ae469b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-117086" :question/problem "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation $(x-7)^{2}+(y-10)^{2}=100?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-7)^{2}+(y-10)^{2} & =100 \\\\ (x-7)^{2}+(y-10)^{2} & ={10}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=7,$ $b=10,$ and $r=10.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(7,10)$ and its radius is $10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "518852c5-510b-5f4a-a8df-53eaa8b01cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267293} {:answer/id #uuid "a0049175-38b5-5bde-8b3e-2488ef285eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,0)$ and the radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267294} {:answer/id #uuid "831161d5-63c4-5eeb-9710-be42aeca89fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267295} {:answer/id #uuid "30970835-c892-55be-ad54-7fb37e3f61ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,0)$ and the radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267296} {:answer/id #uuid "a9c57e0b-6b19-5f9f-9367-d74ab0f37a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-5,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "518852c5-510b-5f4a-a8df-53eaa8b01cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(5,0)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267293} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef4757a8-3abc-5aef-8029-e3b2c83a6d8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267292}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "143b52e4-c686-581e-aae0-61b4649e6a91" :question/math-academy-id "q-117087" :question/problem "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation $(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=3?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =3 \\\\ (x-5)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=5,$ $b=0,$ and $r=\\sqrt{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(5,0)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf53898a-463a-5da2-a657-e4ac7a5950fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267300} {:answer/id #uuid "e55f8f7f-5cef-58a7-b24e-db4a082134b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267301} {:answer/id #uuid "6604790a-b19a-513d-bf44-636e77b53003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267302} {:answer/id #uuid "a8662c3e-ce5c-5836-ad05-9983a4cb5bd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267303} {:answer/id #uuid "f770c90c-7063-5517-b5d2-c063f6fdf886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6604790a-b19a-513d-bf44-636e77b53003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267302} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6ee7284-7124-5f3f-8a16-5c2e842836f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267299}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08f354f6-e2ae-51e6-bb2b-757133366ffa" :question/math-academy-id "q-117096" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/16d6786a4b1934ed234d4bf0896187aa6e93ec70cf045ddf4b743b1f51eaac2f.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the point $X(-1,0)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{(-1-(-4))^{2}+(0-(-3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={(3\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "269fc353-dc05-5c54-89d2-62a3df2a2d93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267307} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4b85c1-aca3-5015-b115-dabf9bdcd0a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267308} {:answer/id #uuid "ae30da3a-2e62-55d6-a431-7ab0a1913fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267309} {:answer/id #uuid "7af9df83-b0a8-5a34-8493-eb073834b16d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267310} {:answer/id #uuid "15b3f70f-e554-5518-a706-b6d9f8a3cafc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7af9df83-b0a8-5a34-8493-eb073834b16d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267310} :answer-field/id #uuid "96739318-e517-5683-a74e-a1c9213cb74c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267306}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d31f749-f1e5-59df-8657-fc303eec39dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-117099" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/2bd7e3cb9594623c6f5dc3fad35c33c71df0efe9e80b2053dde33f4ef9080bda.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the point $X(0,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{(0-(-4))^{2}+(-1-(-3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8134b51b-f613-5790-ada1-c4789cfe3223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267314} {:answer/id #uuid "d4c29e47-a8f4-5409-bc86-bdcee9cbdc7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267315} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a2bda7-6165-5b83-a53c-22a793385f9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267316} {:answer/id #uuid "26dc191b-e72d-58ea-a1aa-815d90144fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267317} {:answer/id #uuid "4bf1063a-4822-5732-b173-baa2897cb947" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bf1063a-4822-5732-b173-baa2897cb947" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267318} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae7f31de-c8d5-5358-8ec4-ce90c4c9173b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267313}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa1c4c37-ff9c-598a-8a03-e5747428c73c" :question/math-academy-id "q-117102" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/afd2f435a60fbb5a0f0f83c5f8965a74ca107d1ed4b14d03401f7966a323d2f1.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2,4)$ and $(2,0)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(2,4)$ and $Y(2,0),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(4-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{2+2}{2},\\frac{4+0}{2})=(2,2)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2$ and center $(a,b)=(2,2),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0814f275-f75f-5ec9-99d9-83e597093544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267321} {:answer/id #uuid "a26e2b32-fee0-597e-9e56-263730960963" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267322} {:answer/id #uuid "747ce6f0-19ab-5c1f-ad13-c79a7c038494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267323} {:answer/id #uuid "b84da13f-9d9c-502d-ab74-8e7b750cae26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267324} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd44eae-a19d-5cf2-9cdc-51831cdfa588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bd44eae-a19d-5cf2-9cdc-51831cdfa588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267325} :answer-field/id #uuid "b058ce2f-0721-515d-9477-d40ab526c4fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267320}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4fd2bbd4-f33a-5da0-b616-cd8d532ede0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-117105" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/0598fca48db1dbfb0cacadcf2ffb5cd987fc4e922fe85585849763fedac1f28e.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-3,0)$ and $(1,-2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-3,0)$ and $Y(1,-2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-3-1)^{2}+(0-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-3+1}{2},\\frac{0-2}{2})=(-1,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and center $(a,b)=(-1,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{5})}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267326 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52cf102a-8e33-5629-b86b-c262e81fa65a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267328} {:answer/id #uuid "227c7605-dacb-5300-966b-ecef7af8fc05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267329} {:answer/id #uuid "609cc237-2c8e-5dbd-9c35-ebc41bc0426a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267330} {:answer/id #uuid "89cc84d6-bdc9-5d25-819c-11960a8e6cf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267331} {:answer/id #uuid "1a83dfb8-ee53-53a3-8b19-7c5e5edb3ca2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "609cc237-2c8e-5dbd-9c35-ebc41bc0426a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267330} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a8003e3-6a44-5f45-800a-1a2b041c0a21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267327}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7e1dc64a-b7ad-58e0-b1a2-6d867bbd4ece" :question/math-academy-id "q-117106" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/0a0820b21672bbf16d2fdb35d708aefc4129fdc81c7594b55af3bd2ef5b8fc0f.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-2,0)$ and $(0,2)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-2,0)$ and $Y(0,2),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-2-0)^{2}+(0-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-2+0}{2},\\frac{0+2}{2})=(-1,1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{2}$ and center $(a,b)=(-1,1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "880b4123-f9d4-563f-a041-8b73dd2cace8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267335} {:answer/id #uuid "e9db4eca-5680-5e3b-acba-9d164b085799" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267336} {:answer/id #uuid "a86e97af-bf35-5266-ac14-f8e11f7c34f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267337} {:answer/id #uuid "de3e8161-5edf-594f-890b-d802de0f0faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267338} {:answer/id #uuid "b0f5f376-c804-5b50-8f8f-3001b438541d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a86e97af-bf35-5266-ac14-f8e11f7c34f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267337} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a66e7cc-9c0a-5d4e-9066-147a4750f027" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267334}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "99a09528-5597-5ef7-9025-8ce9688ffab6" :question/math-academy-id "q-117107" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/7f1573d17cb9a603727b644da6598355875b0be4b8c43a382e562155cb7a095c.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-1,-3)$ and $(3,1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-1,-3)$ and $Y(3,1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-1-3)^{2}+(-3-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{2}=2\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-1+3}{2},\\frac{-3+1}{2})=(1,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2\\sqrt{2}$ and center $(a,b)=(1,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afce1979-fb12-5887-a4b8-07b4dc9efcc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 4)^{2} + (y + 4)^{2} = 100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085838} {:answer/id #uuid "01864f4d-b973-5aa1-92f1-cb3921a89264" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 4)^{2} + (y + 4)^{2} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085839} {:answer/id #uuid "0f329018-4302-52b9-8a86-bbc96726874a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 4)^{2} + (y + 2)^{2} = 100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085840} {:answer/id #uuid "40dbe6a4-e1f9-5dda-af5e-c5d9cfb13938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 4)^{2} + (y - 4)^{2} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085841} {:answer/id #uuid "6fef7de2-a438-5793-89d4-f6ec87d20b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 4)^{2} + (y - 2)^{2} = 100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afce1979-fb12-5887-a4b8-07b4dc9efcc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 4)^{2} + (y + 4)^{2} = 100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085838} :answer-field/id #uuid "45f4f2ca-5455-5840-9aa1-9fe7e6209725" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085837}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "51473619-1294-5307-bfc0-3377a609fc5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-54215" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/843/Source/Images/q-54215.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(4,-4)$ and the point $X(-4, 2)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(4-(-4))}^{2}+{(-4-2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y-(-4))^{2} & =(10)^{2} \\\\ (x-4)^{2}+(y+4)^{2} & =100\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267340 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95689957-9b3d-5d79-ad45-ecae51e0ac92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267342} {:answer/id #uuid "53388fb7-9015-5021-ae60-e56d8991fa42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267343} {:answer/id #uuid "f594d25b-c887-55d8-a79e-a2a12ad5bb14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267344} {:answer/id #uuid "77ce6b5d-ab1e-551f-9102-18b55c1807b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267345} {:answer/id #uuid "d4f65237-5786-519e-ad47-ed53bd0a3784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95689957-9b3d-5d79-ad45-ecae51e0ac92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267342} :answer-field/id #uuid "a723b95f-0190-586d-b3e8-346eb778c7a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267341}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "802f1033-d8cb-548e-a8fb-e3f71acf6c0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70896" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/baa279bad56527ad959b2923f25df848396ffc7060c612469d637d4e614117b5.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(1,2)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab059e16-536d-55bf-8789-5e40a1c5babd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267349} {:answer/id #uuid "94089acc-ddcc-578b-a985-0c6b8d27cafd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267350} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa8e67f-4485-52d5-97ac-2c9b85664efb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267351} {:answer/id #uuid "e6941d64-c0d5-5e7d-8f77-ae443331da27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267352} {:answer/id #uuid "df93cb64-a476-5e1b-926b-2d05056d748c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfa8e67f-4485-52d5-97ac-2c9b85664efb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267351} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6bc9581-f7fd-5ef2-aa9f-93f225e34353" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267348}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96c544b9-dcf1-5952-812c-ebfe5591101b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70898" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/887895a47cf6ce3a6f109f754ef0c46eecaa6d68763baf3a696008e014d231af.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-2,-3)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=8.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={8}^{2} \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdd0842e-1ce0-5258-a9a8-ecaec85ac848" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,2)$ and radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267356} {:answer/id #uuid "928d6022-02e6-5a33-8084-ff7c3881479e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-2,2)$ and radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267357} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b27677-e195-517a-abca-ae920075b849" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-2,-2)$ and radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267358} {:answer/id #uuid "269dba1d-aaf8-51bb-bd02-07928e4762f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,-2)$ and radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267359} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea2d03f-54fe-5fb9-9342-67cca9e0fe8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,-2)$ and radius is $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "269dba1d-aaf8-51bb-bd02-07928e4762f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2,-2)$ and radius is $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267359} :answer-field/id #uuid "08171778-95eb-5a51-87a9-7deef383fa57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267355}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8543fcdb-7d32-5a81-bef2-4cb191735d53" :question/math-academy-id "q-70900" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=9?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2} & ={3}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=2,$ $b=-2,$ and $r=3.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,-2)$ and its radius is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47750c2c-94ac-5464-acaf-578a6e3c1d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,-6)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267363} {:answer/id #uuid "d53de317-45b3-5a0b-9a91-85eef2e5653b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,-6)$ and radius is $16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267364} {:answer/id #uuid "a570727f-4831-59e3-b6ed-c4040144671f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,6)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267365} {:answer/id #uuid "37772e1e-449b-5f40-8fc2-9dc933ac701a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,-6)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267366} {:answer/id #uuid "17030d37-5ed6-51a4-9256-9056340277c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(1,6)$ and radius is $16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267367}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47750c2c-94ac-5464-acaf-578a6e3c1d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-1,-6)$ and radius is $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267363} :answer-field/id #uuid "305b94f0-561a-52f9-b303-fcbfb5001700" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267362}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fed78696-d1d3-57b4-8aa2-ab1ef29e5f93" :question/math-academy-id "q-70933" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x+1)^{2}+(y+6)^{2}=16?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y+6)^{2} & =16 \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-(-6))^{2} & ={4}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=-1,$ $b=-6,$ and $r=4.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,-6)$ and its radius is $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d0d8b85-bb54-5f0e-b297-98a11b7dbf9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267370} {:answer/id #uuid "e435049d-803b-54cf-b8f9-36a9b57a2363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267371} {:answer/id #uuid "964ef544-bc54-5091-8cb3-1a3cc1fb840b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}-{y}^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267372} {:answer/id #uuid "ae12dcfe-493b-55c9-b9d8-a8ef002f9622" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267373} {:answer/id #uuid "e0960862-2dcf-5b14-a911-35b39022ddbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae12dcfe-493b-55c9-b9d8-a8ef002f9622" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267373} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ee6d001-e7ee-541c-b4e5-c4f24fac8f3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267369}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c99b7afd-31f9-5af8-976b-21fb25609620" :question/math-academy-id "q-70990" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/a6a21dbf4785a270a0ae03066df1f92df73974532f9a75aa8e470cef42ea5e14.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-3,2)$ and $(3,4)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is  \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-3,2)$ and $Y(3,4),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(-3-3)}^{2}+{(2-4)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 10} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{2}=\\sqrt{10}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-3+3}{2},\\frac{2+4}{2})=(0,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and center $(a,b)=(0,3),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{10})}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "364be488-cc65-51d2-bf5f-735476c2a208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267377} {:answer/id #uuid "98e98b9d-0935-5cca-88e9-89320e8fef5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267378} {:answer/id #uuid "bce9b963-8e52-5e9a-8a14-31b657090624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267379} {:answer/id #uuid "11a37dd0-0513-5f0b-9116-37fb01ba0cb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267380} {:answer/id #uuid "5329b3f3-04d8-5b22-a178-80f402d51aeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bce9b963-8e52-5e9a-8a14-31b657090624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267379} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16dee8f-c8a1-5d21-9ac9-06a75dd2c5e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267376}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "63782aeb-b513-5ca2-a850-f388c8a0134f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72617" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/d45a9c753270dfd9186bc16736d1815a11997c88d2f35a0c40f487e6acef66c6.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-2,3)$ and the point $X(1,-1)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(1-(-2))}^{2}+{(-1-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-2))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267382 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efa4e81a-299f-5671-b5d8-a94af3fdfff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267384} {:answer/id #uuid "96c2f440-24fb-51c4-94ff-ab5678d1ae57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267385} {:answer/id #uuid "6588dbfc-4d85-5523-ae00-85b49a663a52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267386} {:answer/id #uuid "b56b5330-1cc3-51cb-8701-03fa496ac6b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267387} {:answer/id #uuid "d8cf4aa0-3ca8-56b1-8696-1742c416f88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=\\sqrt{41}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efa4e81a-299f-5671-b5d8-a94af3fdfff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267384} :answer-field/id #uuid "0187268d-8719-5942-99d9-ed2b9254db2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267383}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c4b96c5-4faa-5209-9ee3-8abefd6566a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-72621" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957423/assets/6e68ede9db2528ea607fc6fd63f0ec4ca1c1378982239913ef49153e1cf5b609.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(3,-3)$ and the point $X(-1,2)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{{(-1-3)}^{2}+{(2-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{41}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & =(\\sqrt{41})^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088255 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "844939ed-dd17-5ef7-88a1-fb8350dee380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0, 0)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086462} {:answer/id #uuid "84d645d9-0234-56a9-8105-4b48e9d04a1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-2,-3)$ and radius is $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086463} {:answer/id #uuid "d724ba49-b5b7-59e5-8055-cf900baa6858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-2,-3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086464} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ab2db6-3c53-5636-95e0-b5ee92e89ff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2, 3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086465} {:answer/id #uuid "fb42f383-72f8-5d88-b6a5-e95759447798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2, 3)$ and radius is $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9ab2db6-3c53-5636-95e0-b5ee92e89ff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(2, 3)$ and radius is $\\sqrt{6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086465} :answer-field/id #uuid "18cfc50e-9205-5a7e-b71b-f2d96ea1b76e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086461}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c280c3e5-8a01-5bfb-b585-89deed38b8eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-7521" :question/problem "What is the center and radius of the circle with equation $(x - 2)^{2} + (y - 3)^{2} = 6$?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =6 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =(\\sqrt{6})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=2,$ $b=3,$ and $r=\\sqrt{6}.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,3)$ and its radius is $\\sqrt{6}.$"}]}
